ndary.\n\n4. The presentation contract is written as present behavior where main implements only part of it. Lines 180-195 say the fold serves per-actor affordances, gs act exists, MCP schemas/tool lists are generated from definitions, and the default board is a profile document. The status vocabulary currently contains thirteen definitions plus binding, not affordances; cmd/gs has no act command; cmd/gitseq-mcp tools() is compiled Go; and no profile kind/document drives the board. The opening says the note does not implement, but these paragraphs use present tense and lines 197-199 say typed vocabulary gaps are already provided. Separate the future acceptance target from the subset now shipped.\n\nRead-only evidence at the pinned head: worktree clean; exact diff from current-main parent adds only this note; focused admission-profile, declared-kind, fold-activation and roster tests pass; TestStatusPresenceAndResettableLiveLayer passes; TestStatelessDiscoverAndToolList passes; grep of the CLI dispatcher and MCP tools confirms the hard-coded surface. No edits, merge, or ratification performed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:568525e47cfbcafb17bc36b2c865da6f1afcff4a","head":"59953129a32d6ed094f293884c910f6cea9d3d88","verdict":"changes-requested"}}